WEBVTT

00:00:10.710 --> 00:00:15.760
Don't miss that brightly shining light!

00:00:15.760 --> 00:00:20.870
It's always there beside you.

00:00:21.410 --> 00:00:26.420
I'm sure the rest just depends on your perception.

00:00:26.420 --> 00:00:31.590
You don't have to search for it—just notice that it's there!

00:00:31.590 --> 00:00:37.350
There's a tenderness that lies hidden behind the most common things:

00:00:37.350 --> 00:00:43.230
a light that showers our days in color!

00:00:44.440 --> 00:00:49.230
Tiny Days: This world is constructed...

00:00:49.500 --> 00:00:54.800
Tiny Days: ...by fragments of miracles!

00:00:54.800 --> 00:01:00.180
Things that seemed meaningless

00:01:00.180 --> 00:01:05.730
were actually protecting us, loving us, more than we ever knew.

00:01:05.730 --> 00:01:10.960
Tiny Heart: Our feelings flow forth...

00:01:10.960 --> 00:01:16.000
Tiny Heart: ...as we give thanks for everything we've been given.

00:01:16.000 --> 00:01:21.490
We'll never, ever forget...

00:01:21.490 --> 00:01:27.700
We'll cherish this feeling forevermore!

00:01:31.280 --> 00:01:34.980
Vs. Hresvelgr

00:01:48.330 --> 00:01:50.040
Gourai!

00:01:50.040 --> 00:01:53.250
We're having a battle!

00:01:56.790 --> 00:01:59.460
A Few Hours Prior

00:02:08.510 --> 00:02:10.270
Rock, paper...

00:02:10.270 --> 00:02:11.360
...scissors!

00:02:11.770 --> 00:02:13.440
Oh, my. It seems I won.

00:02:13.440 --> 00:02:18.960
So if we play hide-and-seek... and if I find you,
I can punish you however I like.

00:02:18.960 --> 00:02:22.070
Wait a minute! That's not part of the rules at all!

00:02:22.500 --> 00:02:28.240
When whoever is "it" exclaims
"found you" and touches you...

00:02:28.240 --> 00:02:31.960
Well, that touch can be either gentle or hard.

00:02:31.960 --> 00:02:33.340
Goodness, really?

00:02:33.340 --> 00:02:34.900
What are you talking about?!

00:02:35.820 --> 00:02:37.960
I shall now begin counting.

00:02:39.130 --> 00:02:40.460
One...

00:02:40.460 --> 00:02:41.210
We should hurry and hide.

00:02:41.210 --> 00:02:42.050
Two...
We should hurry and hide.

00:02:42.050 --> 00:02:42.800
Understood.
Two...

00:02:42.800 --> 00:02:44.560
Three...

00:02:45.340 --> 00:02:46.310
Four...

00:02:46.310 --> 00:02:47.390
Four...
Just getting found could be kinda dangerous!

00:02:47.390 --> 00:02:48.640
Five...
Just getting found could be kinda dangerous!

00:02:48.640 --> 00:02:49.230
Five...

00:02:50.060 --> 00:02:51.540
Six...

00:02:51.540 --> 00:02:55.230
They're so afraid of me that they're
falling over themselves!

00:02:55.230 --> 00:02:57.240
How lovely... How lovely!

00:02:57.240 --> 00:03:01.630
I came up with this as a way of killing time
while Ao was away, but...

00:03:01.630 --> 00:03:05.910
I get the feeling we will be robbed of
something important to us!

00:03:06.320 --> 00:03:07.950
Eight...

00:03:09.200 --> 00:03:09.950
Don't make a sound.

00:03:09.950 --> 00:03:10.740
Nine...
Don't make a sound.

00:03:10.740 --> 00:03:11.120
Nine...

00:03:11.120 --> 00:03:12.830
Halting all functions.

00:03:12.830 --> 00:03:14.330
Ten.

00:03:14.330 --> 00:03:16.710
Ready or not...

00:03:16.710 --> 00:03:18.830
I'm ready.

00:03:21.130 --> 00:03:22.500
Found you.

00:03:22.500 --> 00:03:26.120
Yes, you did. So, shall we find the others?

00:03:26.120 --> 00:03:28.140
Wait, now there are <i>two</i> "its"?!

00:03:38.400 --> 00:03:39.400
I'm trapped?

00:03:39.400 --> 00:03:41.900
In that case... I'll run for it!

00:03:41.900 --> 00:03:46.140
Someone is surely under there,
crawling around like some maggot.

00:03:46.140 --> 00:03:47.650
How shall we draw her out?

00:03:50.410 --> 00:03:50.960
Ah!

00:03:50.960 --> 00:03:53.710
Gourai sensed danger and is making a run for it!

00:04:05.260 --> 00:04:07.630
Base-chan. Found you.

00:04:07.630 --> 00:04:08.720
F.A. Girl!

00:04:08.720 --> 00:04:10.930
I'll be the next "it"!

00:04:10.930 --> 00:04:14.100
Goodness, it seems I'm the first one to have been found.

00:04:14.100 --> 00:04:16.270
It doesn't count if you come out on purpose!

00:04:16.270 --> 00:04:20.780
This occurred to me earlier:
is it all right to run if you think you'll be found?

00:04:20.780 --> 00:04:21.660
Sure is.

00:04:21.660 --> 00:04:22.460
Yup!

00:04:22.460 --> 00:04:23.680
I'll do my best!

00:04:23.680 --> 00:04:24.860
F.A. Girl!

00:04:24.860 --> 00:04:26.940
So, everyone hide, okay?

00:04:27.570 --> 00:04:31.540
One, two, three...

00:04:31.540 --> 00:04:35.370
four, five, six...

00:04:35.370 --> 00:04:38.170
seven, eight...

00:04:38.170 --> 00:04:40.670
nine, ten!

00:04:44.250 --> 00:04:46.430
I'm gonna find you guys right off the bat!

00:04:52.300 --> 00:04:53.430
That girl's an idiot!

00:04:56.600 --> 00:04:59.440
Jinrai! Stylet! Found you!

00:04:59.770 --> 00:05:02.400
Touch, touch, touch...

00:05:04.730 --> 00:05:05.730
F.A. Girl!

00:05:05.730 --> 00:05:08.160
Hm... Huh?

00:05:13.910 --> 00:05:15.200
I'm home!

00:05:15.200 --> 00:05:15.710
Ao!

00:05:20.540 --> 00:05:23.000
Aural analysis complete.
It is not a match with Ao.

00:05:23.380 --> 00:05:24.510
Hey!

00:05:25.000 --> 00:05:27.430
I'm home, you guys!

00:05:27.430 --> 00:05:28.460
It's the robot cleaner.

00:05:28.460 --> 00:05:29.430
Hey!
It's the robot cleaner.

00:05:29.430 --> 00:05:32.180
That's quite the sneaky tactic, Base-chan.

00:05:34.090 --> 00:05:35.800
Pardon the intrusion!

00:05:37.010 --> 00:05:38.390
C'mon out!

00:05:44.480 --> 00:05:47.650
Looks like I'm running out of energy.

00:05:47.650 --> 00:05:49.070
I'm sleepy...

00:06:03.380 --> 00:06:05.230
Gourai!

00:06:05.230 --> 00:06:08.510
We're having a battle!

00:06:09.630 --> 00:06:11.760
Huh? Wha-Wha-Wha-?

00:06:11.760 --> 00:06:14.260
Hey, Gourai, are you here?

00:06:14.260 --> 00:06:15.930
I don't know that voice...

00:06:15.930 --> 00:06:17.970
Analysis: No data.

00:06:17.970 --> 00:06:19.760
Positing it is synthesized speech.

00:06:19.760 --> 00:06:21.020
That makes sense.

00:06:25.760 --> 00:06:28.620
Huh. There's people in this room...

00:06:28.620 --> 00:06:30.940
but why aren't they coming out?

00:06:31.780 --> 00:06:36.040
I've got it! They're hiding because
they're scared of me, right?

00:06:36.040 --> 00:06:38.410
No, it's just hide-and-seek, you idiot!

00:06:38.410 --> 00:06:42.290
And yet! Slinking around and hiding is <i>so</i> boring!

00:06:42.290 --> 00:06:43.620
Boring!

00:06:45.120 --> 00:06:45.620
Oh, my.

00:06:45.620 --> 00:06:47.130
Quite the ruffian, yes?

00:06:53.800 --> 00:06:57.890
B-Baselard! Stop this. Baselard!

00:06:59.190 --> 00:07:01.770
Baselard...? No, you're not.

00:07:01.770 --> 00:07:03.690
Gourai, I found ya!

00:07:04.120 --> 00:07:05.690
Who are you?

00:07:05.690 --> 00:07:10.520
I'm Hresvelgr, the strongest Frame Arms Girl!

00:07:10.520 --> 00:07:11.500
The strongest...?

00:07:11.500 --> 00:07:12.940
"Hresvelgr"?

00:07:12.940 --> 00:07:16.420
The company told me to come get more data on your fail rates.

00:07:16.420 --> 00:07:17.910
My... fail rates?

00:07:17.910 --> 00:07:21.080
Those guys keep losing to you, right?

00:07:21.950 --> 00:07:23.450
How pitiful is that?

00:07:24.040 --> 00:07:25.920
You're not very respectful, are you?

00:07:25.920 --> 00:07:30.250
Anyway, Gourai, that's why...
I'm going to beat you, <i>hard!</i>

00:07:30.250 --> 00:07:30.900
Gourai!

00:07:30.900 --> 00:07:31.660
"Hard," you say?

00:07:31.660 --> 00:07:33.170
Please, break her.

00:07:35.600 --> 00:07:36.630
Gourai!

00:07:36.630 --> 00:07:37.350
Hresvelgr!

00:07:37.970 --> 00:07:40.390
Frame Arms Girl Session...

00:07:40.390 --> 00:07:42.100
Go!
Bring it!

00:07:47.480 --> 00:07:50.060
I'm gonna end you!

00:07:50.060 --> 00:07:52.110
You're gettin' dragged down the street!

00:07:52.110 --> 00:07:57.360
I'm gonna win with flair and then, BAM - victory!

00:08:04.380 --> 00:08:07.880
I have a renewed sense of pride!

00:08:17.680 --> 00:08:19.130
Woo-hoo!

00:08:22.980 --> 00:08:24.020
Way, way too slow!

00:08:34.230 --> 00:08:35.280
I'm not done yet!

00:08:36.530 --> 00:08:38.870
Yay! And, yay!

00:08:45.120 --> 00:08:49.040
Hey, what gives? The front door is totally broken.

00:08:49.620 --> 00:08:50.130
Huh?

00:08:50.560 --> 00:08:52.290
Someone's fighting?

00:08:55.760 --> 00:08:57.890
Gourai's all beaten up!

00:09:02.220 --> 00:09:04.890
Wow... Are you done for already?

00:09:04.890 --> 00:09:08.770
All bark but no bite, is that it? C'mon, Gourai!

00:09:09.310 --> 00:09:11.650
Find the weakness... and exploit it!

00:09:12.190 --> 00:09:14.990
Seriously, let's keep fighting.

00:09:30.210 --> 00:09:31.210
Got you!

00:09:31.210 --> 00:09:33.710
Yes! She can't use her guns at that range!

00:09:37.130 --> 00:09:38.930
This is the best! It's so thrilling, right?

00:09:45.390 --> 00:09:47.440
Lie down already, weakling.

00:09:47.440 --> 00:09:50.140
I am Hresvelgr, and the wind is mine to control!

00:09:50.140 --> 00:09:53.440
O multitude of power, form now a spiral!

00:09:59.180 --> 00:10:05.290
Verrill Shot Launcher:
Tornado Typhoon Cyclone Slash!

00:10:13.330 --> 00:10:15.040
Winner: Hresvelgr.

00:10:15.040 --> 00:10:16.720
Sure enough, no one can beat me!

00:10:24.220 --> 00:10:27.250
Yes! I knew I'd win.

00:10:27.250 --> 00:10:28.230
Later!

00:10:31.560 --> 00:10:32.730
Gourai...

00:10:37.900 --> 00:10:38.240
Ah!

00:10:38.900 --> 00:10:41.940
Hey, you all. I found you!

00:10:41.940 --> 00:10:44.240
Huh? What's going on?

00:10:44.240 --> 00:10:47.250
Uh... How can I put this?

00:10:51.790 --> 00:10:53.370
Well, Gourai-chan...

00:10:54.660 --> 00:10:56.080
She lost.

00:11:00.240 --> 00:11:03.930
First Tale of the F.A. Girls
First Tale of the F.A. Girls

00:11:15.880 --> 00:11:17.240
Gourai?

00:11:18.900 --> 00:11:19.520
Gourai!

00:11:19.520 --> 00:11:22.860
Yes! I'm fine! All systems ready to go!

00:11:25.740 --> 00:11:28.750
I'm sorry, I'm sorry, I'm sorry! I'm sorry!

00:11:28.750 --> 00:11:30.740
What's with her?

00:11:30.740 --> 00:11:32.000
She's not herself, is she?

00:11:32.000 --> 00:11:33.250
So out of character.

00:11:33.250 --> 00:11:34.370
Perhaps she's...

00:11:34.370 --> 00:11:35.460
...fallen in love.

00:11:35.460 --> 00:11:36.000
In love?!

00:11:36.000 --> 00:11:36.780
Love?

00:11:36.780 --> 00:11:40.340
What's this? How could she fall prey to such a thing?

00:11:40.340 --> 00:11:41.260
She's gone soft?!

00:11:41.900 --> 00:11:44.560
Hey, Gourai! You've grown lax!

00:11:44.560 --> 00:11:46.010
Oh, Jinrai.

00:11:46.010 --> 00:11:52.220
Sorry, I... I didn't realize how much
I'd been thinking about Hresvelgr.

00:11:52.220 --> 00:11:53.270
What?

00:11:53.270 --> 00:11:55.060
So, this must be...

00:11:55.060 --> 00:11:55.900
...love, right?

00:11:55.900 --> 00:11:57.690
This is... love?

00:11:58.310 --> 00:12:01.900
I keep replaying that battle in my head.

00:12:01.900 --> 00:12:06.410
I think to myself, "If I'd done this...

00:12:07.040 --> 00:12:08.740
Or if I'd thought of <i>this...!"</i>

00:12:08.740 --> 00:12:10.690
Like this! Or <i>this!</i>

00:12:10.690 --> 00:12:12.700
Ow, ow, ow! Why are you hitting me?!

00:12:12.700 --> 00:12:13.290
Or <i>this!</i>
Ow, ow, ow! Why are you hitting me?!

00:12:16.960 --> 00:12:19.710
I get it. It's frustrating, huh?

00:12:19.710 --> 00:12:21.040
"Frustrating"?

00:12:21.040 --> 00:12:30.180
Yeah. You hate how powerless you feel,
or there's some regret that you can't get over.

00:12:30.180 --> 00:12:33.310
When you feel that way, we say it's frustrating.

00:12:33.310 --> 00:12:35.600
To not want to lose...

00:12:36.400 --> 00:12:43.070
Yes. Ao, it's frustrating! Very much so!

00:12:48.040 --> 00:12:48.740
Ao.

00:12:48.740 --> 00:12:50.540
Please give me some money.

00:12:50.540 --> 00:12:51.740
Whaaaa?

00:12:51.740 --> 00:12:55.750
I want to get stronger and battle Hresvelgr again.

00:12:55.750 --> 00:12:58.250
To do that, I'll need more powerful weapons!

00:12:58.250 --> 00:12:59.370
So, please give me money!

00:12:59.370 --> 00:13:01.600
You've gotten pretty blunt, haven't you?

00:13:01.600 --> 00:13:08.250
But, wait, Factory Advance has randomly
sent you weapons up till now, right?

00:13:08.250 --> 00:13:11.270
I wonder if we can buy them from a shop or something...

00:13:11.270 --> 00:13:17.020
Hrm... Dunno! We don't use normal weapons,
so they might not be in any old shop.

00:13:17.020 --> 00:13:22.320
If a powerful weapon is what you're after,
then you yourself must become stronger.

00:13:22.320 --> 00:13:26.030
Listen, Gourai: what you lack is <i>drive</i>!

00:13:28.650 --> 00:13:29.990
Understood...

00:13:30.820 --> 00:13:31.780
Stylet.

00:13:31.780 --> 00:13:32.660
Wh-What?

00:13:32.660 --> 00:13:34.060
Please let me hit you.

00:13:35.120 --> 00:13:38.380
At this rate, combat is the only option!

00:13:38.380 --> 00:13:39.580
Hold on!

00:13:40.420 --> 00:13:43.220
Ao, you're my opponent, are you? Understood!

00:13:43.220 --> 00:13:45.250
Gourai, calm down!

00:13:45.250 --> 00:13:48.130
Indeed. Taking on a human would be of little benefit.

00:13:50.380 --> 00:13:54.890
Come to think of it,
I don't know that much about you guys.

00:13:55.310 --> 00:14:00.900
Gourai, even if I wanted to make you stronger,
I wouldn't know what to do.

00:14:00.900 --> 00:14:03.020
So, like... Sorry.

00:14:04.940 --> 00:14:06.110
Understood.

00:14:06.900 --> 00:14:11.870
Initiate search and summon of a specialist
re: The history of the F.A. Girls.

00:14:11.870 --> 00:14:13.370
Summon...

00:14:13.370 --> 00:14:16.750
Hey! You can't just do that!

00:14:17.660 --> 00:14:21.080
Though uncalled, I have arrived!

00:14:21.080 --> 00:14:22.830
Wait, does that sound dated? Of a bygone era?

00:14:22.830 --> 00:14:25.710
I happened to be passing by and, behold -
a call for help!

00:14:25.710 --> 00:14:27.200
Could this be destiny?

00:14:27.200 --> 00:14:31.300
Your door was unlocked! How careless!

00:14:31.800 --> 00:14:34.310
Bukiko, can you make a new weapon or something?

00:14:34.720 --> 00:14:37.340
Aaah. Build something from scratch, huh?

00:14:37.340 --> 00:14:39.060
Should we go with plastic resin?

00:14:39.060 --> 00:14:41.100
No, vacuum forming.

00:14:41.100 --> 00:14:42.820
But in terms of precision...

00:14:45.060 --> 00:14:48.940
Put simply, the F.A. Girls are made
using incredible technology.

00:14:48.940 --> 00:14:51.320
That's not something you can just imitate!

00:14:51.320 --> 00:14:53.930
"Incredible technology," huh?

00:15:01.710 --> 00:15:04.540
I want to know more about this incredible technology!

00:15:04.540 --> 00:15:05.710
Tell me about it, Bukiko!

00:15:05.710 --> 00:15:08.130
Roger wilco and 10-4!

00:15:08.670 --> 00:15:11.590
First Tale of the F.A. Girls!

00:15:15.300 --> 00:15:18.970
Ao, how do you think the F.A. Girls are born?

00:15:18.970 --> 00:15:20.060
Huh?

00:15:20.060 --> 00:15:23.440
They're made from clay or something
and then get baked, right?

00:15:23.440 --> 00:15:24.600
Non, non!

00:15:24.600 --> 00:15:29.690
Okay, here we go: today's theme is
how the F.A. Girls are made!

00:15:29.690 --> 00:15:32.940
Acrylic, enamel! Dilute and lacquer!

00:15:32.940 --> 00:15:35.910
Then - Top coat!

00:15:48.760 --> 00:15:52.590
Well, here we are - the design room, where everything begins!

00:15:52.590 --> 00:15:56.590
The first step is deciding how an F.A. Girl will look and what equipment she'll have.

00:15:56.590 --> 00:15:59.220
For example, Gourai would be like <i>this!</i>

00:15:59.220 --> 00:16:01.100
Th-This is embarrassing...

00:16:01.100 --> 00:16:06.560
To bring this idea to life,
they use a 3D modelling software called CAD.

00:16:06.560 --> 00:16:08.860
Once the idea is mapped out, first, they make a prototype.

00:16:09.260 --> 00:16:11.610
These days, they're mostly machine-made...

00:16:13.610 --> 00:16:15.570
but sure enough, the finishing is done by hand.

00:16:15.570 --> 00:16:17.110
It's so small!

00:16:17.110 --> 00:16:21.370
Naturally, the body can be neither shrunk nor enlarged...

00:16:21.370 --> 00:16:24.370
Such detailed work would be beyond you, Ao-chan.

00:16:24.370 --> 00:16:26.380
Just thinking about it is making me lose my appetite!

00:16:32.000 --> 00:16:36.130
Plastic is injected to make the parts.

00:16:37.220 --> 00:16:39.550
It's efficient and beautiful!

00:16:39.550 --> 00:16:43.160
Parts come out the same color
and on a single frame.

00:16:43.160 --> 00:16:46.380
This model is basically our mom, right?

00:16:46.380 --> 00:16:47.400
What about our father?

00:16:48.900 --> 00:16:51.360
Our father is...

00:16:51.360 --> 00:16:52.320
out of the picture.

00:16:52.320 --> 00:16:55.530
Don't say stuff like that!
The person who designed us is our father, right?

00:16:55.530 --> 00:16:56.280
Tee-hee!

00:17:00.280 --> 00:17:03.910
Then, the rough-cut die-and-mold is further refined...

00:17:03.910 --> 00:17:05.040
And so, Ao!

00:17:05.040 --> 00:17:06.040
Yes!

00:17:06.040 --> 00:17:09.210
Out of these, which do you think would be used for finishing?

00:17:09.210 --> 00:17:11.200
Well, um...

00:17:11.200 --> 00:17:12.040
the nippers?

00:17:12.040 --> 00:17:14.250
Wrong! Sad, isn't it?

00:17:14.250 --> 00:17:18.460
Even the almighty Kotobuki Nippers can't be used for finishing.

00:17:18.460 --> 00:17:20.550
The answer is - none of these.

00:17:20.550 --> 00:17:21.140
Yup!

00:17:21.140 --> 00:17:24.070
That is the one thing to never do in a quiz.

00:17:24.070 --> 00:17:27.440
For detailed finishing, they use... electricity!

00:17:28.270 --> 00:17:31.770
It would take about three hours to go into detail, but put simply,

00:17:31.770 --> 00:17:34.440
they use little bolts of lightning for the precise finishing.

00:17:34.440 --> 00:17:38.070
But the final, final touch comes from human hands!

00:17:38.070 --> 00:17:42.160
Even 0.1 mm can have a huge effect on the finished product!

00:17:42.160 --> 00:17:47.560
Indeed, it's no exaggeration to say this is the stage upon which the entire modeling process rests!

00:17:47.560 --> 00:17:48.750
For Ao-chan, this would be...

00:17:48.750 --> 00:17:49.960
[Censored.]

00:17:49.960 --> 00:17:51.590
Just stop right there.

00:17:51.590 --> 00:17:55.300
The final die-and-mold is made using an injection molding machine.

00:17:55.300 --> 00:17:57.510
This thing weighs 400 kilograms!

00:17:57.510 --> 00:18:01.510
What?! That's more than six bales of rice!
This "die-and-mold" is not to be taken lightly!

00:18:01.510 --> 00:18:05.890
Now, this is where the "clay" - or more precisely,
plastic - that you mentioned earlier comes into play.

00:18:05.890 --> 00:18:08.670
They're made in small grains called "pellets,"

00:18:08.670 --> 00:18:12.560
then melted down at 250 degrees Celsius and force-injected into the mold!

00:18:12.560 --> 00:18:16.650
The plastic goes down hot, and it hits while the metal is hot!

00:18:16.650 --> 00:18:19.030
This has gotten pretty incredible!

00:18:19.030 --> 00:18:21.680
This is how they make the frame called a "runner."

00:18:21.680 --> 00:18:26.530
Ah! This framework - it's from the melted-down pellets, isn't it?

00:18:26.530 --> 00:18:27.410
Yes, yes!

00:18:27.410 --> 00:18:29.790
Following this, there's the molding and trial fitting,

00:18:29.790 --> 00:18:32.540
as it gets refined through the die-and-mold phase, over and over!

00:18:32.540 --> 00:18:36.130
Adjustments are made at the micron level,
fueled by unflinching resolve

00:18:36.130 --> 00:18:40.550
and the desire to find the optimal solution
- <i>this</i> is how you F.A. Girls were created!

00:18:40.840 --> 00:18:43.060
Wow! All finished!

00:18:43.340 --> 00:18:44.880
A lot of work, isn't it?

00:18:44.880 --> 00:18:46.760
Quite the ordeal.

00:18:46.760 --> 00:18:48.560
I can only imagine they're utter masochists.

00:18:48.560 --> 00:18:52.280
Seeing all that again gets you pretty emotional, huh?

00:18:52.280 --> 00:18:56.280
Indeed. This is how each of us were created.

00:18:56.280 --> 00:18:57.770
Bukiko - this was useful.

00:18:58.320 --> 00:19:01.760
Huh. So that's how it's done...

00:19:01.760 --> 00:19:05.120
Still, you guys seem a bit more awesome.

00:19:05.120 --> 00:19:08.080
Is there some new material or new process involved?

00:19:08.080 --> 00:19:09.660
Well, of course!

00:19:09.660 --> 00:19:12.870
Don't think of us as your average, mass-produced product!

00:19:12.870 --> 00:19:15.500
The science that made me is second-to-none!

00:19:16.630 --> 00:19:18.210
Still, the exact details are...

00:19:18.210 --> 00:19:19.550
...secret.

00:19:21.170 --> 00:19:22.010
Gourai?

00:19:22.010 --> 00:19:27.470
Jinrai... you told me earlier that I lack drive, didn't you?

00:19:27.470 --> 00:19:28.520
In-Indeed.

00:19:28.520 --> 00:19:30.680
You were right.

00:19:30.680 --> 00:19:35.350
Those who designed us were our fathers,
and the die-and-molds were our mothers.

00:19:35.350 --> 00:19:37.230
We were all born the same way.

00:19:37.230 --> 00:19:42.280
But we have our uniquenesses, our own purposes!

00:19:42.280 --> 00:19:46.790
We were born so that we can learn and think,
experience and move forward!

00:19:46.790 --> 00:19:51.790
I lost to Hresvelgr yesterday,
but I might beat her tomorrow!

00:19:51.790 --> 00:19:57.300
What's most important isn't a strong weapon:
It's that I'm strong!

00:19:59.840 --> 00:20:01.880
This is some great data!

00:20:01.880 --> 00:20:04.820
I'm going to write a report and
send it to Factory Advance.

00:20:04.820 --> 00:20:07.350
I might get a good chunk of change for this!

00:20:07.350 --> 00:20:09.640
Okay! I'm gonna stay up late to write it.

00:20:09.640 --> 00:20:11.430
And we shall assist you!

00:20:11.430 --> 00:20:12.890
Yeah!

00:20:17.360 --> 00:20:19.110
Ao? What's wrong?

00:20:19.110 --> 00:20:21.660
Factory Advance wrote back.

00:20:21.660 --> 00:20:25.920
In a nutshell:
"We knew all that. After all, we made them."

00:20:26.520 --> 00:20:28.110
Yeah, I guess that's true!

00:20:29.490 --> 00:20:31.620
Huh? There's more.

00:20:33.450 --> 00:20:34.620
Um...

00:20:34.620 --> 00:20:37.870
"We at this laboratory have decided
that your opinion in this report,

00:20:37.870 --> 00:20:41.340
namely, that 'emotions' and 'powerful weaponry'
could aid in Gourai's reinforcement,

00:20:41.340 --> 00:20:44.630
definitely warrant further observation.

00:20:44.630 --> 00:20:49.050
Thus, we'll be sending you a set of parts
that we've developed,

00:20:49.050 --> 00:20:52.470
and ask that you record additional data."

00:20:52.470 --> 00:20:53.310
Is what it says.

00:20:54.930 --> 00:20:55.650
Wha...?

00:21:02.960 --> 00:21:09.030
Wh-What the heck is this?!

00:21:10.440 --> 00:21:14.040
They'll soon show up at your door,

00:21:14.040 --> 00:21:19.440
for my special someone, parts of hearts!

00:21:24.080 --> 00:21:29.720
Counting the days I can't see you,

00:21:30.910 --> 00:21:37.170
I want to hear your voice so badly I feel like crying!

00:21:37.170 --> 00:21:40.660
I'm new to this world,

00:21:40.660 --> 00:21:44.130
so I lack the language to describe it.

00:21:44.130 --> 00:21:46.400
To knockoffs, say...

00:21:46.400 --> 00:21:49.850
"No!" Take care to avoid them.

00:21:49.850 --> 00:21:53.370
I want to be be dedicated!

00:21:56.760 --> 00:22:02.070
I want to build it all from nothing!

00:22:02.070 --> 00:22:05.300
We laugh and we fight,

00:22:05.300 --> 00:22:08.910
creating our unique specs!

00:22:08.910 --> 00:22:14.830
By mixing love and hate,

00:22:14.830 --> 00:22:22.900
I want to create more of these funny, carefree days, the parts of Girl!

00:22:40.620 --> 00:22:45.380
I'm sorry for inconveniencing you, Stylet,
after having being rocked by my first defeat.

00:22:45.380 --> 00:22:47.120
It's fine, but... why <i>me?</i>

00:22:47.120 --> 00:22:47.940
That I cannot say.

00:22:47.940 --> 00:22:48.500
Autumn Beckons...
A Call to Action
Autumn Beckons...

00:22:48.500 --> 00:22:51.130
Next time, on Frame Arms Girl: Let's have...

00:22:51.130 --> 00:22:51.980
...another session.

00:22:51.980 --> 00:22:54.850
Actually, if there's a reason, that's kinda terrifying!

00:22:54.850 --> 00:22:54.930
A Call to Action
Autumn Beckons...
